# std/ls — one of the file tools (std/files holds the source they share).
# The help is a HERE-STRING so it lives in this expression, which is stripped
# from the tree the build sees: editing the docs re-keys this tool's ArgTree and
# nothing it builds from.
HELP=<<END
List a directory: one entry per line, directories (and source trees) with a trailing `/`. `root` is the directory or source tree: a path in the session (`.` for its top), or `<hash>[/<path>]` for one that is not in the session, such as an evaluated caos-std/. Prefer this over `ls` via bash. Listings are cut at 1000 entries.
@root
END
IMAGE=run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/rustc --src:@=DEEP-DEPS/files
curry --base=$IMAGE --op=ls --help=$HELP
